               1                     MODULE mod_eos_ocean
               2                     ! Hi Ben:
               3                     ! I think that the best place to look for what you want is the following site.
               4                     ! http://www.marine.csiro.au/~jackett/eos/
               5                     ! It provides efficient algorthms for the density and other thermodynamic properties of standard seawater.
               6                     !
               7                     !  The most accurate representations for density that are currently available can be found on the TEOS-10 website
               8                     !  which can be found by searching for TEOS-10 in google.  This site provides a wealth of information on the equation of state
               9                     !  and thermodynamics of seawater -- including an approach to include the influence of composition  anomalies on the density of seawater.
              10                     !
              11                     ! Dan
              12                     ! The second site is more comprehensive and provides the "best available" information, but the first may be adequate for what you are looking for.
              13                     !
              14                     ! I hope this helps.
              15                     !
              16                     ! Regards,
              17                     !
